    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "a",
    "value": "11"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-10b-2015-p12.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "The squared distance from \\((x,-x)\\) to \\((5,5)\\) is \\[ \\begin{aligned} &(x-5)^2+(-x-5)^2 \\\\ &= 2x^2+50. \\end{aligned} \\]\n\nBeing inside or on the circle means \\(2x^2+50\\le100\\), so \\(x^2\\le25\\). Thus \\(-5\\le x\\le5\\), giving \\(11\\) integer values.\n\nThus, the correct answer is A.",
      "hints": [
        "Substitute \\((x,-x)\\) into the distance formula from \\((5,5)\\)",
        "Solve \\(2x^2+50\\le100\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
